  "goodToKnow": "Das Exil is exile: ins Exil gehen, im Exil leben. After the Nazis came to power in 1933, many German writers, artists and scientists went into exile, including Thomas Mann, Bertolt Brecht, Albert Einstein and Marlene Dietrich. Their work is called Exilliteratur. Germany's Article 16a grants political asylum, partly as a lesson from this history. Der Exilant is an exile (person). Stress: ek-SEEL. Plural: die Exile."
